---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Long Press is a daily tech brief by Swami, eleven years leading product at Condé Nast and Newsweek. Five stories each morning, plus a column on what stays broken."
  wide
>
  <!-- Masthead -->
  <div class="page-head" id="about-head">
    <span class="eyebrow">Masthead</span>
    <h1>About Long Press</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">
      Long Press publishes two things. <strong>The Daily Five</strong> lands at 10:00 IST with the five tech stories worth your time, each one taken apart the same way. <strong>Known Issue</strong> is the column, and it goes after the things that have been broken for a while that nobody is fixing.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Founder & Editor Profile -->
  <div class="about-profile" id="who-writes-it">
    <div class="about-profile__avatar" aria-hidden="true">
      <img src="/images/about/swami-headshot.jpg" alt="" width="72" height="72" loading="eager" />
      <span class="about-profile__status" title="Desk active &middot; Writing daily"></span>
    </div>

    <div class="about-profile__content">
      <div class="about-profile__byline">Editor &amp; Publisher</div>
      <h2 class="about-profile__name">Swami Guru</h2>
      <p class="about-profile__bio">
        Swami spent eleven years leading product at Condé Nast &mdash; <em>Vogue</em>, <em>GQ</em>, <em>Wired</em>, <em>Condé Nast Traveller</em> and <em>Architectural Digest</em> &mdash; and before that at Newsweek and Metro World News. Twenty brand launches across five continents. Long Press is written from inside that job, by someone who sat in the rooms where these decisions get made and knows which half of an announcement is the half that matters.
      </p>

      <div class="about-profile__actions" id="publisher">
        <a href="https://www.builtbyswami.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="chip">
          BuiltBySwami &nearr;
        </a>
        <a href="https://www.builtbyswami.com/work-with-me" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="chip">
          Advisory Practice &nearr;
        </a>
        <a href="mailto:builtbyswami@gmail.com" class="chip">
          builtbyswami@gmail.com
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- The Two Core Editorial Pillars & Philosophies -->
  <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="products-title" style="margin-top: var(--s7);">
    <div class="column-section-title">
      <h2 id="products-title">The two things Long Press publishes</h2>
      <span>How each one works</span>
    </div>

    <div class="about-pillars-grid">
      <!-- Pillar 1: The Daily Five -->
      <div class="about-pillar-card" id="cadence">
        <span class="about-pillar-card__eyebrow">Pillar 01 &middot; The morning brief</span>
        <h3>The Daily Five</h3>
        <p>
          Five tech stories every morning at <strong>10:00 IST</strong>, each one taken apart the same way. Five is a cap, not a target. More than five things happen most days and most of them do not matter, so the work is deciding what to leave out.
        </p>
        <div class="about-pillar-card__philosophy">
          <h4>Every story, taken apart the same way</h4>
          <p style="font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-bottom: 8px;">Every item in the brief answers the same four questions:</p>
          <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 18px; font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-soft);">
            <li><strong>The problem:</strong> What was annoying, expensive or broken before this.</li>
            <li><strong>What changed:</strong> What actually shipped, with the dates, prices and numbers, minus the adjectives.</li>
            <li><strong>The catch:</strong> The subscription, the region it is not available in, the line in the footnote. There is nearly always one.</li>
            <li><strong>What it means for you:</strong> Whether to act on it, wait, or ignore it.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <a href="/daily" class="dispatch-card__link" style="margin-top: auto; padding-top: 12px;">
          Read the archive &rarr;
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Pillar 2: Known Issue -->
      <div class="about-pillar-card" id="known-issue">
        <span class="about-pillar-card__eyebrow">Pillar 02 &middot; The column</span>
        <h3>Known Issue</h3>
        <p>
          In software, a known issue is the bug everyone has agreed to live with. This column is about the other kind: the things in Apple, Google, Meta, Android, iOS and the apps you use daily that have been wrong long enough to count as a decision rather than an oversight. Not launch reviews. The brief handles those.
        </p>
        <div class="about-pillar-card__philosophy">
          <h4>How it differs from the brief</h4>
          <p style="font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-bottom: 8px;">No embargo access to protect, so nothing to soften:</p>
          <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 18px; font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-soft);">
            <li><strong>Not today&rsquo;s news.</strong> The brief is set off by something that happened this morning. A column is set off by something that has been true for months.</li>
            <li><strong>Plain about the money.</strong> Who benefits from the thing staying broken is usually the answer, and usually the part nobody prints.</li>
            <li><strong>The operator&rsquo;s read.</strong> Eleven years leading product inside large publishers, which is mostly an education in why obvious fixes do not ship.</li>
            <li><strong>A verdict.</strong> Buy it, skip it, or wait. Not &ldquo;it depends&rdquo;.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <a href="/known-issue" class="dispatch-card__link" style="margin-top: auto; padding-top: 12px;">
          Read the column &rarr;
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Standards & Ethics -->
  <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="standards-title" style="margin-top: var(--s7);">
    <div class="column-section-title">
      <h2 id="standards-title">Editorial Standards &amp; Ethics</h2>
      <span>How this works</span>
    </div>

    <div class="about-standards-grid" id="corrections-and-contact">
      <div class="about-standards-card">
        <h3>Visible Corrections Policy</h3>
        <p>
          Mistakes get fixed on the page, with a line saying what changed and when. Nothing gets quietly edited away. If you find something wrong, write to the desk.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-standards-card">
        <h3>Commercial Opportunities &amp; Independence</h3>
        <p>
          Long Press takes sponsorships, newsletter placements and advisory work. Anything paid for is labelled as paid, every time, and the opinion is not part of the deal. For rates, write to <a href="mailto:builtbyswami@gmail.com">builtbyswami@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Syndication and Feeds -->
  <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="syndication-title" style="margin-top: var(--s7);">
    <div class="column-section-title">
      <h2 id="syndication-title">Read it elsewhere</h2>
      <span>Feeds and search</span>
    </div>

    <div class="column-manifesto" style="margin: var(--s4) 0 var(--s6);">
      <div class="column-manifesto__card">
        <span class="column-manifesto__num">RSS 2.0</span>
        <h3>RSS</h3>
        <p>Every brief and every column, the moment it publishes. Summaries rather than full text, so you still come to the page.</p>
        <a href="/rss.xml" class="dispatch-card__link" style="margin-top: 8px;">Subscribe to RSS &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <div class="column-manifesto__card">
        <span class="column-manifesto__num">Search Index</span>
        <h3>Archive search</h3>
        <p>Search every issue and column by keyword, company or topic.</p>
        <a href="/search" class="dispatch-card__link" style="margin-top: 8px;">Search the archive &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <div class="column-manifesto__card">
        <span class="column-manifesto__num">JSON</span>
        <h3>The search index</h3>
        <p>The index the search page runs on. It is public, if you want to build something with it.</p>
        <a href="/search.json" class="dispatch-card__link" style="margin-top: 8px;">See the JSON &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Contact Callout -->
  <div class="column-tip-box" id="contact" style="margin-bottom: var(--s8);">
    <h3>Contact the desk</h3>
    <p>
      Tips, corrections, or a story about something quietly broken where you work: <a href="mailto:builtbyswami@gmail.com">builtbyswami@gmail.com</a>. Published from Bengaluru (IST).
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
